From 254e17dc5b54e5341de91d4f9755a3b652a9ee2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:13:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] dt-bindings: pinctrl: qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi: add SM6225

The LPASS LPI TLMM in SM6225/Khaje matches the SM6115 variant
already supported by pinctrl-sm6115-lpass-lpi: 19 GPIOs, the same
pin/function table (SoundWire TX on gpio0-2, SoundWire RX on
gpio3-5, DMIC01/23 on gpio6-9) and a separate slew-rate register
block. The vendor FDT exposes the same slew offsets for the
SoundWire pins gpio0-5 that the SM6115 driver encodes.

Allow boards to describe the controller as
"qcom,sm6225-lpass-lpi-pinctrl" with the SM6115 fallback, so no
driver change is needed. This is a binding-only change; the
device tree using it remains disabled and no LPI or SoundWire
probe has been verified on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Port <port@local>
---
 .../bindings/pinctrl/qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl.yaml     | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl.yaml
index f4cf2ce86..df5fcfb4e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pinctrl/qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl.yaml
@@ -16,7 +16,11 @@ description:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl
+    oneOf:
+      - const: qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl
+      - items:
+          - const: qcom,sm6225-lpass-lpi-pinctrl
+          - const: qcom,sm6115-lpass-lpi-pinctrl
 
   reg:
     items:
